Once you've done the minimum damage to be able to
enhance, it's supposed to mark that column to say so.
Once you've maxed out your skill in a type, it's supposed
to say so with a different character.  Supposed to is all
well and good but my observation is the code that
generates the displayed list doesn't work correctly.

> Is there a limit to the number of weapons a wizard can enhance? =A0Is it
> only one?

There is no such limit.  With wizards it's often a bad idea
to waste skill slots on weapons classes other than
dagger but that's a matter of managing a limited resource.

> Are weapon enhancements meted out with separate limits?

Skill slots from both weapons and spells are drawn from
the same pool.

I see 2 possibilities:

1) You're using the polearm at range 1 as a wielded melee
weapon and getting 1d4 damage from the shaft.  That
damage does not count against the skill.  (a)pply at range
2 to use the pole arm.  When training pole arm weapons
(usually spetum as soon as I get one from a troll) I like to
use it on lit levels of the mines or anywhere else I have
room to manuever.

2) It's a bug in the skill class display or counters.  Since
I have seen bugs in skill class displays in vanilla 3.4.3 it
would not surprise me this is a bug.


